{"id":"u-4cbe6507-ef64-4964-88e8-77892d0a4b27","src":"community","title":"Squat Dead","author":"Mez","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/9lVlDM-squat-dead","desc":"I made this to focus on strength building through the Squat and Deadlifts, its a four week wave loading program built around your Training Max. All you need to do is input 90% of your 1RM for the Squat and Deadlift the program will increase the weight each week before reducing back down on the fourth for a deload to then continue back up. Increase weight by 2.5kg if you find the sets easy. By week 9 look to increase your Rep Maxes 2.5kg as the cycle starts again. When you first start it will ask you to input numbers for things like Paused Deadlift or Temp Squat. Keep these numbers true to your actual 1RM.\n\nI designed this to incorporate a fourth training day set for fitness which is not included here. For me this is a repeatable conditional piece which will change after every fourth week. For example;\n\n30 Sec Max Effort Sprints\n4 Mins Slow Walk.\nRepeat six rounds.\n\nThe 5th week will be a new conditioning piece, reacted weekly until the 8th week. The fitness element is entirely up to you.  I wont add any conditional work other than the example above. Take or leave the Volume sessions, the real work is all in the Squat and Deadlift days.\n\nThe Volume sessions are purely there for maintenance. Adjust this to suit depending on how you feel after the strength days. The primary focus here is the strength side of the program. Volume here is the muscle builder so make the reps good, make them slow and watch your form. All sets and Reps should be manageable. Reduce weight accordingly but ideally you should aim to work to failure by the final set. The volume sessions should give a fairly decent builder in the other muscle groups should you not be incorporating these on your fitness day. \n\n-----\n\nI hope you enjoy the program structure and variability. Please do leave your feedback I will read and adjust accordingly. 🙏","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-10-21T20:32:59.522Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Squat Day DELOAD","Volume  Day","Deadlift Day DELOAD"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Low Bar)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":85},{"r":2,"pct":90},{"r":1,"pct":95}]},{"n":"Squat (Paused)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":65,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Dip (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Tricep Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Kelso Shrug","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Y T W","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":6.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":85},{"r":2,"pct":90},{"r":1,"pct":95}]},{"n":"Deficit Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":70,"x":3}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Wide Grip Pull-Up","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Glute-Ham Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":7.5,"x":3}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Low Bar)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":87.5},{"r":2,"pct":92.5},{"r":1,"pct":97.5}]},{"n":"Squat (Paused)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":70,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7